# nr-mcp — Custom Node-RED MCP Server

Custom Python MCP server replacing buggy `mcp-node-red` npm package.
Fixes the critical `PUT /flow/:id` tab reorder bug with safe GET→POST deploy.

## Architecture docs (read at start of each session)
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — design decisions, Node-RED flow structure, current state
- `docs/TOOL_SPEC.md` — all 7 tools with parameters, returns, error codes
- `docs/INSTALL.md` — installation via uv tool install

## Notion references (via Notion MCP)
- **Task:** `31d5a347-f34c-811e-9b33-cbecaae12a6d` (TASKS DB) — main tracking task
- **MCP plan:** `30a5a347-f34c-815b-a812-ff80faacc43d` — Faza E4 section

## Stack
- Python 3.11+, `mcp` SDK, `httpx` async, `pydantic`, `pydantic-settings`
- Install: `uv tool install` (same pattern as ha-mcp)
- Entry point: `nr_mcp.server:main` (pyproject.toml scripts)

## Target environment
- Node-RED v4.1.6 on Home Assistant (Proxmox VM 101)
- URL: `192.168.1.31:1880` (direct, NOT through HA ingress)
- Auth: Basic Auth (credentials from env vars NR_URL, NR_USER, NR_PASS)
- 14 flow tabs, ~1731 nodes

## CRITICAL: Never use PUT /flow/:id
This is the entire reason this project exists. Node-RED's PUT endpoint reorders tabs.
Always use: GET /flows → modify in-place → POST /flows with rev (optimistic locking).
See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` section "Deploy: GET→POST (never PUT)" for details.

